payload.estimate_error:
Under-sized. The slice was first judged size S for the argv repair alone. Build-check moved it to the full loop because SC-028 and SC-037 carried a race and a safety part, and it ran as medium risk with one designer. The actual run was 3 designs (one cut off by the provider's weekly limit), 4 critiques, 3 builds, 6 code reviews and 4 validations. The builds changed 27, 15 and 10 files. The cost came from classes of input the sizing never counted:
- argv grammar classes: unpaired quotes (IN-M1), partly quoted program names (IN-m1), dash-leading path pieces (O-053);
- link kinds at the temporary name: hardlink, file symlink, dangling symlink, junction, directory symlink;
- folder-rights shapes: 11 rows in ReportFileFolderRightsCorpus.json, one of which, the create-only drop folder F03, disproved the probe precondition.
Risk 'medium' fits the file count but not the parser and ACL surface. Treat any slice that rewrites CommandLine.Arguments or the ReportFile rights logic as high risk.
